{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794558841882,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf6bc5bffePiQWy1Q3jiC9P1","part":{"partID":"prt_1d40ad2af001BDhsMjacQrfmqj","sessionID":"ses_e2bf6bc5bffePiQWy1Q3jiC9P1","messageID":"msg_1d40abc20001OAK7mI9F6Vg6Me","type":"tool","id":"call_efb2111585bd4e22b6fdf000","tool":"grep","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/commands/doctor/assets","pattern":"runtime cop|pointer"},"output":"Found 29 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json:\n  Line 641:       \"consumer\": \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs\",\n\n  Line 645:       \"why\": \"The gate 1 pointer block is generated from the first line naming this module, so repository text placed above Gate 1 would take over every runtime mirror.\"\n\n  Line 654:       \"consumer\": \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs\",\n\n  Line 658:       \"why\": \"The Cursor rule's second block is generated from the first line holding this marker, so repository text placed above Gate 2 would take over the command pointer.\"\n\n  Line 672:       \"why\": \"The gate names its machine contract by file and by the function it exports, so the pointer and the exported symbol have to keep naming each other.\"\n\n  Line 742:         \"pointer\"\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml:\n  Line 29:     - \"CLAUDE.md, folded into the block and replaced by a one-line @AGENTS.md pointer by default. Kept as it is, with its lines still moved into the block, when --keep-claude-md was given. Created as that pointer when it is absent and the run writes another file.\"\n\n  Line 32:     - \".cursor/rules/skill-routing.md, rewritten by its own generator, sync-gate1-pointers.cjs, which this engine calls and never composes a byte of\"\n\n  Line 51:   pointer_generator: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs, called by the engine and never by this workflow\"\n\n  Line 64:   keep_claude_md: \"--keep-claude-md folds a divergent CLAUDE.md into the block and keeps the file. --remove-claude-md folds it and leaves a one-line @AGENTS.md pointer, which is the default (default false, so the pointer).\"\n\n  Line 101:       - \"Exit 0 means the write ran. Keep exactly the lines the engine printed: its apply line, one wrote or removed line per path, the pointer-sync line, the repo-rules line after a router write, the preservation line, the check-after line, the backup line, the undo line, one copy line per overwritten file and STATUS=OK.\"\n\n  Line 102:       - \"A nonzero pointer-sync line is the one verdict the run leaves unresolved: the generator rewrites an existing .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md and never creates a missing one, so a repository without that file ends with exit 1 and the mirror still missing. Keep the line as printed, render it in the result's Pointer sync: field, never list .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md in Files changed on the strength of the allowlist that names it, and render a Next: line naming /doctor:runtime-mirrors, whose rows list each generated mirror that drifts with the write form of its checker. The repair chain for the pointer file itself is the presentation's troubleshooting row for A10, because that route does not check it. A repo-rules line that reports an error belongs in Router: the same way.\"\n\n  Line 117:       - \"When the write ran and read back, render the presentation contract's embedded result with the paths the engine wrote or removed, the pointer-sync and repo-rules lines as they printed, the backup folder, the re-read verdict, the undo block the engine printed and the next line those lines name.\"\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-git-hooks.yaml:\n  Line 94:       - \"If the script refuses the key (exit 2), render its reason, add the presentation's pointer for that switch, and return to phase_2_present\"\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:\n  Line 71: The twelve rows are A1 install state, A2 sections present, A3 order and numbering, A4 section currency, A5 pins, A6 delivery budget, A7 repo-local block, A8 unmarked repo-unique content, A9 unmarked local edits, A10 runtime copies, A11 REPO RULES.md and A12 template purity. Read A1 first: it says which state the repository is in, and every other row is a detail of that state. A8 and A9 are the two rows that name a line somebody wrote, so quote them in full.\n\n  Line 183: Pointer sync: [the engine's pointer-sync line]\n\n  Line 189: Next: [the repair the lines above name, or none: a nonzero pointer-sync ends here with /doctor:runtime-mirrors]\n\n  Line 193: A nonzero `pointer-sync` line is not a verified mirror, and the run's `STATUS=OK` covers the files it wrote and nothing else. The generator rewrites an existing `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` and never creates a missing one, so on a repository that has no such file the line reads `exit 1 … missing` and the file is still absent when the run ends: it is never one of the files this run wrote, it never appears in `Files changed`, and the allowlist naming it is not evidence that it was written. Show `Pointer sync:` exactly as the engine printed it, show the run's own `STATUS=OK`, and let `Next:` carry the route that names the drifting mirror: `/doctor:runtime-mirrors`. What has to happen before that mirror can be written is in the troubleshooting table, because the file has to exist before the generator has a block to put in it.\n\n  Line 268: | `A10` reports a runtime copy out of sync, or the apply's `pointer-sync:` line reported a nonzero exit | The generator rewrites an existing `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` and never creates a missing one, so a missing file stays missing however often the embed reruns. `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` lists the generated runtime mirrors that drift, each with the write form of the checker that owns it; the pointer block is not one of the files that route checks, so a `missing` line on it means the file has to exist first. Create `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`, run `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs --root <root>`, then rerun `/doctor:agents-md check` and read `A10` again |\n\n  Line 284: | The apply's `pointer-sync:` line reported a nonzero exit | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` | It lists each generated runtime mirror that drifts with the write form of its checker, and `A10` names the copy that is still unverified |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-speckit-retrieval.yaml:\n  Line 153:     detection: \"One of the five runtimes has no path to the Gate 1 lookup instruction: the root AGENTS.md line is missing, the generated pointer block in .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md is absent or differs from that line (sync-gate1-pointers.cjs --check exits 1), or Pi's context-file loading no longer lists AGENTS.md\"\n\n  Line 155:     note: \"Claude reads the root AGENTS.md directly, Pi loads it from the working directory and Codex loads it as the project instructions of this repository; the Cursor rule shared by Cursor and Devin carries a generated pointer block. Reach is per runtime: a pointer, direct load, verified inheritance, or session-start injection each count as a path.\"\n\n  Line 183:       - \"Gate 1 reach, per runtime: verify the root AGENTS.md instruction that Claude reads directly, Pi loads from the working directory and Codex loads as project instructions; run node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs --check for Cursor and Devin through .