{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794558860281,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf6bc5bffePiQWy1Q3jiC9P1","part":{"partID":"prt_1d40b19b5002BODdp0tc1G34FG","sessionID":"ses_e2bf6bc5bffePiQWy1Q3jiC9P1","messageID":"msg_1d40af387001R5kSrq3j2IFXU7","type":"tool","id":"call_2053d6dedaa841789739b695","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"^- \\[.\\] T02[4-9] \" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/tasks.md"},"output":"111:- [ ] T024 Report a link where the checklist expects no file (`CHK`, `CHKT`). Test first: in `CHKT`, add a case on the `pure` fixture with `.codex/AGENTS.md` linked to `../AGENTS.md`: expect that entry's `state` `FINDING` and `kind` `symlink where none belongs`. Today it is `PASS` `symlink`. Then in `copyVerdict`'s symlink branch, before `pointsAtRoot` is read, return `{ state: FINDING, kind: 'symlink where none belongs', detail: 'links to <link>, where the checklist expects no file' }` when `expectsAbsent`. Verify: before the change the case fails on `PASS`, after it `NT $CHKT` reports `fail 0` and `node $CHK | rg -c \"^STATUS=OK\"` prints 1.\n112:- [ ] T025 Describe a pointer as it is tested (`CHK`, `CHKT`). Test first: in `CHKT`, add a case on the `pure` fixture whose `CLAUDE.md` holds `@AGENTS.md` and the line `Use the house style.`: expect the entry `kind` `pointer` with a detail reading `names AGENTS.md and carries no shipped line`. Today it reads `every line names AGENTS.md`. Then change the pointer detail to `names <root> and carries no shipped line`. Verify: before the change the case fails, after it `NT $CHKT` reports `fail 0` and `rg -c \"every line names\" $CHK` prints nothing.\n113:- [ ] T026 Count a missing pointer apart from the copies as expected (`CHK`, `CHKT`). Test first: in `CHKT`, add a case on the `pure` fixture with no `CLAUDE.md`: expect the A10 detail to end `, 1 pointer missing` and its leading count to leave the `CLAUDE.md` entry out. Today the entry is counted as expected. Then in `rowRuntimeCopies`, leave entries of kind `pointer missing` out of the expected count and append `, <n> pointer missing` when there is one. Verify: before the change the case fails, after it `NT $CHKT` reports `fail 0`, `node $CHK | rg \"^A10\"` prints a line starting `A10 runtime copies: 5/6 copies as expected, 1 pointer missing` and `node $CHK | rg -c \"^STATUS=OK\"` prints 1.\n114:- [ ] T027 Report a router row of the wrong width as malformed (`CHK`, `CHKT`). Test first: in `CHKT`, add a case whose `REPO RULES.md` is a complete router with one trigger row's last cell holding `a | b`: expect A11 to print `malformed trigger row at line <n>: 4 cells where the header has 3`, no `missing` line for that row's rule and state `FINDING`. Today A11 prints `missing trigger row for` that rule. Then make `parseTableRows` return every row with its line number and a `malformed` flag, have `missingRows` read every row's cells and have `rowRouter` print one `malformed <kind> row at line <n>: <cells> cells where the header has <width>` line per malformed row and report `FINDING` when one exists. Verify: before the change the case fails, after it `NT $CHKT` reports `fail 0`, `node $PL/probe-router-widths.cjs` prints `mismatched lines []` twice and `node $CHK | rg -c \"^STATUS=OK\"` prints 1.\n115:- [ ] T028 Say four child checks and describe the new embed exits (`CHK`, `DSR`). In the header of `CHK`, change `Three of the twelve rows` to `Four of the twelve rows` and add that the source template's purity belongs to the manifest generator's check. In `DSR`'s `agents-md-check.cjs` row, change `Three of them run their owner as a child` to four and name the generator's check. In `DSR`'s `agents-md-embed.cjs` row, add that apply restores and fails on a foreign line as on a dropped one, refuses a symlinked `REPO RULES.md` or Cursor mirror it would write and exits 3 when a write fails after the backup, having restored from it or said why not. Verify: `rg -c \"Four of the twelve rows\" $CHK` prints 1, `rg -c \"Three of them\" $DSR` prints nothing, `rg -c \"exits 3\" $DSR` prints 1 and `node --check $CHK` exits 0.\n118:- [ ] T029 Refuse a flag value that is another flag (`CK`, `CKT`). Test first: in `CKT`, add a case running `node $CK --root --json`: expect exit 2. Today it prints `SKIP no-codex-hooks` and exits 0. Then make `parseArgs` return `null` when the value after `--root` or `--config` starts with `-`, as `HW` does. Verify: before the change the case fails on exit 0, after it `NT $CKT` reports `fail 0`.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"111:- [ ] T024 Report a link where the checklist expects no file (`CHK`, `CHKT`). Test first: in `CHKT`, add a case on the `pure` fixture with `.codex/AGENTS.md` linked to `../AGENTS.md`: expect that entry's `state` `FINDING` and `kind` `symlink where none belongs`. Today it is `PASS` `symlink`. Then in `copyVerdict`'s symlink branch, before `pointsAtRoot` is read, return `{ state: FINDING, kind: 'symlink where none belongs', detail: 'links to <link>, where the checklist expects no file' }` when `expectsAbsent`. Verify: before the change the case fails on `PASS`, after it `NT $CHKT` reports `fail 0` and `node $CHK | rg -c \"^STATUS=OK\"` prints 1.\n112:- [ ] T025 Describe a pointer as it is tested (`CHK`, `CHKT`). Test first: in `CHKT`, add a case on the `pure` fixture whose `CLAUDE.md` holds `@AGENTS.md` and the line `Use the house style.`: expect the entry `kind` `pointer` with a detail reading `names AGENTS.md and carries no shipped line`. Today it reads `every line names AGENTS.md`. Then change the pointer detail to `names <root> and carries no shipped line`. Verify: before the change the case fails, after it `NT $CHKT` reports `fail 0` and `rg -c \"every line names\" $CHK` prints nothing.\n113:- [ ] T026 Count a missing pointer apart from the copies as expected (`CHK`, `CHKT`). Test first: in `CHKT`, add a case on the `pure` fixture with no `CLAUDE.md`: expect the A10 detail to end `, 1 pointer missing` and its leading count to leave the `CLAUDE.md` entry out. Today the entry is counted as expected. Then in `rowRuntimeCopies`, leave entries of kind `pointer missing` out of the expected count and append `, <n> pointer missing` when there is one. Verify: before the change the case fails, after it `NT $CHKT` reports `fail 0`, `node $CHK | rg \"^A10\"` prints a line starting `A10 runtime copies: 5/6 copies as expected, 1 pointer missing` and `node $CHK | rg -c \"^STATUS=OK\"` prints 1.\n114:- [ ] T027 Report a router row of the wrong width as malformed (`CHK`, `CHKT`). Test first: in `CHKT`, add a case whose `REPO RULES.md` is a complete router with one trigger row's last cell holding `a | b`: expect A11 to print `malformed trigger row at line <n>: 4 cells where the header has 3`, no `missing` line for that row's rule and state `FINDING`. Today A11 prints `missing trigger row for` that rule. Then make `parseTableRows` return every row with its line number and a `malformed` flag, have `missingRows` read every row's cells and have `rowRouter` print one `malformed <kind> row at line <n>: <cells> cells where the header has <width>` line per malformed row and report `FINDING` when one exists. Verify: before the change the case fails, after it `NT $CHKT` reports `fail 0`, `node $PL/probe-router-widths.cjs` prints `mismatched lines []` twice and `node $CHK | rg -c \"^STATUS=OK\"` prints 1.\n115:- [ ] T028 Say four child checks and describe the new embed exits (`CHK`, `DSR`). In the header of `CHK`, change `Three of the twelve rows` to `Four of the twelve rows` and add that the source template's purity belongs to the manifest generator's check. In `DSR`'s `agents-md-check.cjs` row, change `Three of them run their owner as a child` to four and name the generator's check. In `DSR`'s `agents-md-embed.cjs` row, add that apply restores and fails on a foreign line as on a dropped one, refuses a symlinked `REPO RULES.md` or Cursor mirror it would write and exits 3 when a write fails after the backup, having restored from it or said why not. Verify: `rg -c \"Four of the twelve rows\" $CHK` prints 1, `rg -c \"Three of them\" $DSR` prints nothing, `rg -c \"exits 3\" $DSR` prints 1 and `node --check $CHK` exits 0.\n118:- [ ] T029 Refuse a flag value that is another flag (`CK`, `CKT`). Test first: in `CKT`, add a case running `node $CK --root --json`: expect exit 2. Today it prints `SKIP no-codex-hooks` and exits 0. Then make `parseArgs` return `null` when the value after `--root` or `--config` starts with `-`, as `HW` does. Verify: before the change the case fails on exit 0, after it `NT $CKT` reports `fail 0`.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"^- \\\\[.\\\\] T02[4-9] \\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/tasks.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794558859701,"end":1794558860281}}}}
