{"type":"text","timestamp":1794559088541,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf6bc5bffePiQWy1Q3jiC9P1","part":{"id":"prt_1d40e7b17002P2CUEcN7VVDw5M","sessionID":"ses_e2bf6bc5bffePiQWy1Q3jiC9P1","messageID":"msg_1d40e2dff001nCR57E03CkItWc","type":"text","text":"**T025 complete.** Both named files were edited; no checkbox ticked.\n\nFiles written:\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs` — added `A10 describes a pointer by what it does, not by what every line holds` on the `pure` fixture with `CLAUDE.md` holding `@AGENTS.md` and `Use the house style.`, asserting `kind` `pointer` and detail `names AGENTS.md and carries no shipped line`.\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs` — pointer detail changed from ``every line names ${manifest.root_file}`` to ``names ${manifest.root_file} and carries no shipped line``, and A10 entries now carry `detail: verdict.detail` so the entry itself describes the verdict it records.\n\nVerify output:\n```\nℹ tests 42\nℹ suites 0\nℹ pass 42\nℹ fail 0\nℹ cancelled 0\nℹ skipped 0\nℹ todo 0\nℹ duration_ms 7184.245416\nrg exit=1\n```\n`rg -c \"every line names\" $CHK` printed nothing (exit 1 is ripgrep's no-match status, which is the expected result).\n\nBefore-change run: the new case failed at `assert.equal(claude.detail, ...)` with `actual: undefined`, `expected: 'names AGENTS.md and carries no shipped line'`. The old wording was not reachable through the entry because A10 entries had no `detail` field at all, so the pre-change failure surfaced as a missing field rather than as the old string. Adding the field is what makes the entry detail the task expects observable. After the change the same case passes.\n\nSanity checks: `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs | rg \"^A10|^STATUS\"` printed `A10 runtime copies: 6/6 copies as expected   (PASS)` and `STATUS=OK rows=12 findings=0 unknown=0`. `node --check` passed on both files.\n\nNothing was blocked. Note that `agents-md-check.cjs` and its test already carried the prior lane worker's T024 symlink-guard change in the working tree; I left it in place. No other file was touched and no git state was changed.","time":{"start":1794559081239,"end":1794559088541}}}
